# Grafana Provisioning Repository Rules

## General
- All dashboards are provisioned via JSON files in `provisioning/dashboards/`
- All datasources are provisioned via YAML in `provisioning/datasources/`
- All alerting rules are in `provisioning/alerting/rules/`
- Never commit secrets or API keys — use `${ENV_VAR}` syntax
- Dashboard UIDs must be stable and explicit (never null or auto-generated)
- Set `"editable": false` in all dashboard JSONs — changes via Git only

## Skills — Load based on your task
- Business requirements → `skills/business-analyst/SKILL.md`
- Architecture design  → `skills/system-analyst/SKILL.md`
- SLO/SLI/Alerting     → `skills/sre-engineer/SKILL.md`
- PromQL queries        → `skills/prometheus-querying/SKILL.md`
- Dashboard JSON        → `skills/dashboard-developer/SKILL.md`
- Visual design         → `skills/dashboard-designer/SKILL.md`
- Alert rules           → `skills/alerting-engineer/SKILL.md`
- Datasource configs    → `skills/datasource-engineer/SKILL.md`

## Conventions
- Dashboard tags: `["team:{team}", "tier:{l0|l1|l2|l3}", "domain:{domain}"]`
- Datasource UIDs: `{type}-{env}-{region}` e.g. `prometheus-prod-eu-west`
- Alert UIDs: `{service}-{alertname}` e.g. `payment-api-high-error-rate`
- Runbook URLs must be set for every alert rule
